Package: csmGmmCorr
Type: Package
Title: Correlated Conditionally Symmetric Multidimensional Gaussian Mixtures
    for Composite Null Testing
Version: 1.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Z.", "Liu", email = "ZLiu20@mdanderson.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ryan", "Sun", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the csmGmm method and package on which this package builds"))
Description: Implements the correlated conditionally symmetric multidimensional
    Gaussian mixture (correlated csmGmm) for testing composite null hypotheses
    of the form "more than t nonzero effects" with correlated test statistics.
    The model extends csmGmm (Sun, McCaw and Lin, 2025,
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2024.2422124>) by a common within-feature correlation
    matrix while keeping support-specific weights, support-specific magnitude
    components and the magnitude-ordering constraint. One fit serves
    pleiotropy, same-sign replication and mediation targets for any threshold
    t. Parameters are estimated by a constrained expectation conditional
    maximization algorithm from several starting values; local false discovery
    rates are thresholded by the step-up rule of Sun and Cai (2007). An optional
    monotone adjustment enforces a prespecified ranking order, and an
    extrapolation diagnostic flags discoveries driven by statistics far beyond
    the fitted magnitudes.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats
NeedsCompilation: yes
